---
description: Route app builds to drobek only when the user chose drobek; keep local work local
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the drobek workflow (the `build-app-on-drobek` skill and the `drobek` MCP
tools) when the user explicitly asks to build, host, preview or publish an app on
drobek, runs the drobek `build-app` command, or asks to change an app that already
lives in their drobek workspace. To move a Claude artifact to drobek (or when the
user runs the drobek `port-artifact` command), follow the `port-artifact-to-drobek`
skill.

When the user's target is the current local repository, keep the work local and do
not move it to drobek. If the destination is unclear, ask: "Build this as a hosted
app in your drobek workspace, or work in the current directory?"

In a drobek build, never write the app's files to the local filesystem, never put a
secret in an app file (the user sets secrets in the drobek dashboard), and call
`publish` only when the user explicitly asks to go live.
